# Raw source bytes are the wave's EVIDENCE and are kept on disk for the length of the wave, not
# committed: they are re-fetchable from the URLs recorded in ROSTERS-fayette.md, which also
# transcribes the quotations that matter.
# A trailing comment on a pattern line is NOT a comment -- git reads the whole line, spaces and
# all, as the pattern. Keep every comment on its own line.
#
# What IS committed: ROSTERS-fayette.md, the derived roster and timeline JSON, and the council
# district geometry for all four vintages.

# archived roster, officer, Ballotpedia, news and Wayback pages
*.html
